# Workers Static Assets header rules.
#
# THE SHELL MUST NEVER BE CACHED, AND THIS FILE USED TO MISS THE ONE URL THAT
# MATTERS. The rule below was written for `/index.html` — and the comment above it
# already described the exact symptom it exists to prevent: "a cached shell keeps
# referencing the previous hashed bundle and a deploy 'doesn't show up' until a
# hard refresh". But NOBODY VISITS /index.html; they visit `/`. Measured on the
# live worker:
#
#   /index.html  ->  cache-control: no-cache, must-revalidate      (rule matched)
#   /            ->  cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
#                    cf-cache-status: HIT                          (rule MISSED)
#
# So the root document could be served from Cloudflare's cache, the browser kept
# loading a stale shell pointing at a superseded hashed bundle, and a deploy "did
# not show up" — the very report that prompted this file. A fix that covers the
# path nobody requests is not a fix.
#
# BOTH spellings are listed because `/` and `/index.html` are distinct request
# paths even though they resolve to the same object.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

# Hashed build output is content-addressed — cache aggressively.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
